== Tue Sep 29 07:37:48 IST 2026 typing.log — how the trusted object is defined so that the kernel can evaluate it (BRIEF §2 item 2)

Definition (lean/comparator/ChallengeDeps/I1Witness.lean, namespace I1Witness), R any commutative ring:
  lambdaVecAux (b : ℕ → R) (p : ℕ) : ℕ → ℕ → R           -- FUEL-structural: the first ℕ argument is the fuel
    | 0, _ => 0
    | fuel + 1, n => if n < 2 then 0 else b n * (padicValNat p n : R) - ∑ d ∈ n.properDivisors, lambdaVecAux b p fuel d * b (n / d)
  lambdaVec (b : ℕ → R) (n p : ℕ) : R := lambdaVecAux b p n n     -- fuel := n
Why fuel and not well-founded recursion: a definition by Nat.strongRecOn / WellFounded.fix is compiled through Acc.rec on an
opaque accessibility proof and does not reduce under `decide`; structural recursion on the fuel compiles to Nat.rec (brecOn) and the
kernel unfolds it. Why the fuel n suffices: every recursive call goes to a proper divisor d < n, so the chain n > d > d' > ... has at
most n steps; the solution proves `lambdaVecAux b p f n = lambdaVecAux b p g n` for all f, g >= n (strong induction on n) and from it
the record's recursion as a theorem, `lambdaVec_rec : 2 ≤ n → lambdaVec b n p = b n * padicValNat p n − ∑ d ∈ n.properDivisors,
lambdaVec b d p * b (n / d)` (shipped in the challenge, so the trusted reader sees that the defined object IS the recursion).
e_p(n) := padicValNat p n (the brief's choice) — measured to reduce in the kernel (below); no replacement needed.
epsteinB (n : ℕ) : ℚ := (card of the filter x² + 5y² = n over Finset.Icc (−n) n ×ˢ Finset.Icc (−n) n : ℚ) / 2 — inside a
`noncomputable section` only because the elaborated Preorder ℤ instance path (ConditionallyCompleteLattice...toPreorder) is flagged
noncomputable by the COMPILER; kernel reduction under `decide +kernel` is unaffected (Finset.Icc on ℤ, ×ˢ, filter, card all reduce).
Tactic: `decide +kernel` (kernel evaluation of the Decidable instance; proof term `of_decide_eq_true (Eq.refl true)`; NO
Lean.ofReduceBool, which only `native_decide` introduces).

